WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.036
-Our next guest is
a very funny comedian and actor

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.737
you can see in the film
"Easter Sunday,"

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.906
and who will be headlining
Madison Square Garden

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.176
November 10th as part of
the New York Comedy Festival.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.344
His latest special,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.146
"Jo Koy: Live from
the Los Angeles Forum,"

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:16.716
is streaming now on Netflix.
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.151
-He goes, "Dad,
I'm not gonna throw a party.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:20.419
I promise.
I won't invite anybody."

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:22.154
I go, "Listen to me.
Just hear me out.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:25.191
If you throw a party, Joe,
and one of your friends

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.561
jumps into the pool
and breaks [bleep] --

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.831
breaks their neck,
they're gonna sue me.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.401
And everything
I worked so hard for

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.070
to give to you when I don't --
when I leave this Earth..."

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.204
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.806
"...is gonna go
to Dip [bleep] Dave..."

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.276
"...because he dove
into the shallow end

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.577
at 2:00 in the morning
with the lights off.

00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:47.913
Do you want to give everything
to Dip [bleep] Dave?"

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:50.783
-Please welcome to the show
Jo Koy, everybody!

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.452
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.452 --> 00:01:02.462 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.529 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.031
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:08.167
-Oh, finally, man.
-Yeah! I'm really such a fan.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.637
And I'm so impressed when people
can not just do one of these

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:12.905
but one after the other,
the other.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.774
This is your fourth
Netflix special.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.109
What was the inspiration when
you set out to do this hour?

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.013
-This one, I finally got to --

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.413
I felt like I was in a place

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:23.883
where I can finally
just say everything.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.151
You know?
-That's a nice place to be at.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.419
-Yeah, it --
'Cause it was hard.

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:29.155
In the first special, I --

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.091
you know,
I was turned down by Netflix.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.558
-Yeah.
-And I didn't understand why.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:36.262
And they told me no,
and I went and shot it myself.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.631
I paid for it.
And then --

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.167
No one knows this,
and I keep telling this story,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.669
but it's like -- I had all
the cameras in the building,

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.705
I had the director, I had the
producers all in the building.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.773
We're ready to shoot, and we get
a phone call from Netflix,

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.075
and they go --
and they were like,

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.876
"Hey, we heard you're about
to shoot the special.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:52.979
We just want you to know,
we really don't want it."

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:56.815
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.815 --> 00:01:58.250
And, like, I --

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.886
Just imagine the pressure.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.188
It's like, that was the only
person I wanted to sell it to.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.990
I wanted to sell this
to Netflix,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.191
and they were already saying no.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.459
They haven't even seen it yet.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.461
And backstage, I'm crying,
you know what I mean?

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.863
-Yeah.
-I got all my money invested.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:14.166
And I -- I was gonna shoot it
no matter what.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.436
And I knew once I shot it
and cut it and showed them,

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.072
they were gonna buy it,
and that's what happened.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.741
-What an amazing start
to this whole thing.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.275
And now I'm assuming,
with the fourth one,

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:24.810
you have
a little bit more confidence.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.111
You're probably not crying
before the show.

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:27.947
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.049
And then it was at
the Forum, too,

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.051
so it was like 14,000 people.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.819
And I told the story

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.388
about how they didn't
give me the first one.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.922
-Yeah, there you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:38.524
There you go.
And I would imagine

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.593
the location, the L.A. Forum,
is a cool place to do it

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.295
because you used to --
I mean, your pre-stand-up jobs,

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.297
your pre-acting jobs,
were right around that area.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:48.201
-Exactly!
Hey, thanks, Seth!

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.769
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.871
What?! Thank you.
-I remember, I think I was at

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.340
Nordstrom Rack
when you were working there.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.309
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.978
-I was at Nordstrom Rack!
I had three jobs.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.947
My son was like 1, and I --

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.115
You know,
there's Nordstrom Rack,

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.817
and then right above that
was Borders Books.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.985
-Yep.
-I was just doing

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.420
disposable jobs, so, like,
if I got a gig

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.455
and they wouldn't let me go,
I'm like,

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.090
"All right, I'll just quit."
-Yeah.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.692
-And, uh, and I would drive by
the Forum and just look at it

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:17.230
like, "Oh, that'll never happen,
but I hope it happens."

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.833
And, yeah,
I get "The Tonight Show,"

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.102
I get a standing ovation.
-That's really cool.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.536
-And I didn't know
how many people watched

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:25.838
"The Tonight Show" --

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.608
This is before YouTube
and all that was really big.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.410
And it was like every other
customer walked up to me

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.945
and was like, "Oh, my God!

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.847
You were on 'The Tonight Show'
last night. You were so funny."

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.948
I'm like, "Thank you."
They're like,

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:39.252
"Can I get this in an 8?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.887
-You worked really hard,
and I'm very happy to see

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:44.123
that your teenage son
is also working.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.292
Now, how did he get this job
right here?

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.728
He's on the crew
for the Jo Koy tour.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.296
-Aww.
-Look at that.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.530
That's really cool.
-That's gonna make me --

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.232
Yeah, that's making me sad
to look at it, too.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.501
It's like --
It's a great moment

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.503
to have your kid
on the road with you.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.539
Especially me 'cause, like,
I was a road dog for so long.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.240
-Yeah.
-I missed a lot of birthdays.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.276
I missed a lot of Christmases.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.245
I had to, you know?
And I had to feed him.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.579
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.915
-But now he sees why I did it
and how hard I worked.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.151
-It must be so fun
to be able to do your job

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.419
and also
have family around like that.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.454
-Yes, I love it.
He grounds me.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.657
I don't --
I just want to hang out with him

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.025
as much as I can, and --
-Yeah.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.760
-The cool thing is,
is he's famous.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.262
He has to get the merch out
before they open the doors up,

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:26.398
because he'll be out there for
like two hours taking pictures.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:28.834
But the cool thing is, is I
can't fire him, and he knows it.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.303
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.837
-That's what sucks.
-Yeah.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.338
-Yeah, it's like
I go in my green room,

00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:35.407
and he's laying on the couch.
I'm like, "What are you doing?"

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:38.144
He's like, "Uh, what?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.912
"What are you gonna do,
send me home, Dad?"

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.647
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:45.585
-Speaking of the other side, you
know, obviously you're a parent.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.353
Your mom --
you talk about your mom.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.854
Has she seen it?
-Yeah.

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:50.556
-How does she feel when you talk
about her in your routine?

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.124
-She loves it.
-That's great.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.193
-Yeah, she's love it.
And rightfully so.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.529
She's lived here for so long,
and, you know,

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.232
you live in this country,
and you work hard, and --

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.901
and you go and watch TV,
and you don't see anybody

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.303
that, you know, is being --

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.172
you know, that plays a character
that looks like you

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.074
or sounds like you --
you know what I mean?

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.076
-Yeah.
-For 53 years, she watches TV,

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.044
and she doesn't
see a Filipino ever.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.680
And the one time
she does see it, it's her son.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.115
-Well, that's not bad.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.150
-That's not a bad way
to check that box.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.519
[ Applause ]
-Yeah.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.954
-Speaking of,
you went back and did shows.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.856
You went on tour and you did
shows in the Philippines.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.359
I can't imagine how they feel
when you show up there.

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.427
-That was nuts, man.
The first time I went,

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:31.864
we sold out the arena
and then shot a special there,

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.299
'cause I asked Netflix
if I could shoot one there.

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:36.301
And they let me.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.301 --> 00:05:38.236
And then --
And then, I just recently --

00:05:38.236 --> 00:05:42.108
I was there two weeks ago,
and we sold 10,000 tickets

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.842
on a Wednesday.
-Wow, man.

00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:45.044
That's really something.
-Yeah, it was crazy.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.311
-That is not
an easy thing to do.

00:05:46.311 --> 00:05:47.546
-No.
-But I imagine --

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:48.814
I mean, I feel like
they're getting, you know,

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.583
two for the price of one,
in that they, one,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.484
get to see a comedian they love,
obviously.

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:55.488
And also, you know, it's someone
that they can be extra proud of.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.122
It must be just a great night
for them, as well.

00:05:57.122 --> 00:05:59.058
I'm sure their money well spent.
-Thank you, man, thank you.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.493
-I also wanna --
Before you go,

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.562
you've got a movie,
"Easter Sunday."

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:05.097
-That was crazy!
The way I got "Easter Sunday"

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:08.834
is, my second Netflix special,
"Coming in Hot,"

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.903
Steven Spielberg watched it.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.906
-And then -- And then they
called us in for a general.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.574
And I thought it was just
a general for Amblin.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:16.775
-Yeah.
-And I thought I was just gonna

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.477
go in there, be a general.

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.612
I pitch me, I pitch my story,
they tell me about them,

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:21.747
and then we just leave

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:23.449
and forget the whole thing
happened, right?

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:26.018
And I walk in, and it was like,
every single person's like,

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.386
"Oh, Steven loves you.
Oh, my God.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:28.854
Steven can't stop
talking about your special.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.056
Steven loves you.
Oh, my God.

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:31.424
Steven can't stop
talking about your special."

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:33.025
And I'm like,
to the point where I'm like,

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.727
"Are you talking about
Steven from accounting?"

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.228
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:38.030
"Is there a Filipino
named Steven

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.265
that's bragging about me?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:40.766
"I wanna meet this Steven."

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:42.668
And they were like,
"No, it's Mr. Spielberg,

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.503
and he wants
to make a movie with you."

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.672
And I pitched "Easter Sunday."

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.307
It was a movie I've been
thinking about for a long time,

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.542
and they bought it in the room,
and --

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.311
And it's kind of cool
to have the G.O.A.T....

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.479
-Yeah.
-...be on your side,

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.913
because the minute he bought it,
he was like,

00:06:54.913 --> 00:06:56.515
"Oh, we're making it,
like, now."

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:57.816
And it was that fast.

00:06:57.816 --> 00:07:00.119
He only made "Jurassic World"
and -- and my movie.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:01.387
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.088
And you know how cool that was
to take my son

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:05.691
to watch "Jurassic World"
and, like, my --

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.227
my trailer opened that movie.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:09.962
It was just --
it was such a surreal moment.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.298
-Ah, well,
it's really all well-earned.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:14.099
You put in the hours,
and thank you so much

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:15.835
for making time for us tonight.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.336
-Thank you.
-Jo Koy, everybody!

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:20.773
"Jo Koy: Live from
the Los Angeles Forum"

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.274
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:24.377
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

